{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789799943,"nonce":"OgaIvdDVPNYSww6imSxjbDqdduA=","title":"LLVM: an indirect call through a function address held as an integer panicked","message":"A function value record holds its code address as an i64; the LLVM\nbackend called `into_pointer_value` on it (`zb_call_1`, the one-argument\ncall trampoline) and the promoter thread died, taking every later\npromotion with it. The address is now converted with inttoptr, and a\nvalue that is neither an address nor an integer is a codegen error.","files":null}]}